{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 55, :comments ["<b>For to Me the children of Israel are servants, etc.</b> One needs to know why He repeated, saying ״servants — they are My servants.״ And it appears that He intends to say as follows: ״For to Me the children of Israel are servants״ from their very root — holy from the womb and from pregnancy, in the root of their souls — even had He not brought them out of Egypt; and all this is because they are from Him and to Him. But that which comes from them, to obligate them to hold themselves as servants — ״they are My servants whom I brought out of the land of Egypt״ — for this is a compelling reason for them, and it obligates the attribution of the name of servitude to them." "<b>I am YHWH your Elohim.</b> The reason the verse began speaking in the third person — ״for to Me, etc. … they are My servants״ — and concluded addressing them directly — <b>I am YHWH your Elohim</b> — is perhaps that since He commands the one who purchases a Hebrew slave to send him free in the Jubilee year, therefore He gave him the reason that it is because he is a servant of YHWH, as He said, ״they are My servants.״ And since the purchaser might say that this reason is justified with respect to the slave, that he should not nullify his service and sell himself in perpetuity, but the purchaser has no obligation — and all the more so if he sells himself to a ger toshav or to a resident alien, it is he who transgresses the commandment of YHWH — therefore He concluded, <b>I am YHWH your Elohim</b>, speaking to the purchaser, with whom He began speaking at the beginning of the parashah: ״When you buy״ — and to those whom He commanded directly: ״he shall not rule over him with rigor before your eyes״ — for the word of the King holds sway over them to fulfill everything written."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:01:30.932340921Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}